+@001
+# Causal questions and identification|foundation|technical
+How does intervening on a variable differ from observing it in a causal model?	Build a synthetic three-variable graph and compare conditioning with a defined intervention; consult original causal-model formulations and keep the illustration separate from a real causal finding.
+Why can adjusting for an extra variable introduce bias rather than remove it?	Contrast a common cause with a collider in two explicit causal diagrams; show which paths are opened under stated assumptions rather than recommending adjustment by correlation strength.
+What makes a causal effect identifiable from the available data?	Use two causal explanations compatible with one observational distribution and specify what intervention or assumption would distinguish them; exclude the claim that more samples always resolve identification.
+How can a causal-discovery algorithm produce several equally compatible graphs?	Inspect equivalence classes, conditional-independence tests and hidden-variable assumptions using an original paper and synthetic data; separate graph recovery under assumptions from discovery of real-world mechanisms.
+What must be assumed before answering a counterfactual about one individual?	Contrast population intervention effects with an individual counterfactual in a structural model; expose unobservable assumptions and avoid personal medical or legal predictions.
+# Interpreting model internals and testing explanations|advanced|technical
+What does a feature-attribution map explain when two input features encode the same information?	Compare correlated synthetic features, background distributions and attribution choices; distinguish allocation of predictive credit from causal importance in the world.
+How can a saliency map be tested for dependence on the model it claims to explain?	Plan parameter- and label-randomization controls from original interpretability research; assess changes in the explanation rather than judging only whether a picture looks plausible.
+What evidence is needed before calling a model component a circuit for a behavior?	Trace activation observations, intervention tests, controls and generalization across inputs in a published mechanistic study; distinguish a useful local hypothesis from a complete algorithmic account.
+Why can probing a hidden representation fail to show that the model uses the decoded information?	Compare probe capacity, baselines and causal intervention on a bounded representation task; do not equate decodability with functional reliance.
+How can an explanation remain stable while a model's decision changes?	Specify input perturbations, prediction differences and explanation similarity in a reproducible evaluation; separate explanation robustness from prediction correctness or user satisfaction.
+# Compilers, kernels and measured inference|advanced|technical
+What does kernel fusion remove from an AI inference workload?	Trace intermediate tensors, memory transfers and launch overhead in a documented small computation; benchmark matched precision and shapes without promising universal acceleration.
+Why can a faster attention implementation leave end-to-end response time almost unchanged?	Separate attention time, other operators, queueing and networking in a measured profile; apply an explicit bottleneck calculation rather than attributing all latency to one kernel.
+How do static and dynamic tensor shapes change compilation choices?	Compare tracing, recompilation, padding and graph specialization for a versioned runtime; distinguish compile time from steady-state execution and include irregular workloads.
+What does a roofline model reveal about a memory-bound inference operation?	Relate arithmetic intensity, measured bandwidth and attainable compute using an illustrative operator; document hardware and precision rather than treating peak specifications as observed performance.
+How can changing numerical precision alter both speed and reproducibility?	Compare tolerances, accumulation, supported operators and task outputs under controlled settings; exclude declaring numerical agreement proof of equal downstream quality.
+# Scientific models and domain-specific evaluation|advanced|science
+What does a protein-structure prediction fail to establish about a protein's biological function?	Plan comparison of coordinates, confidence, conformations, interactions and experimental assays using original structure papers; exclude inferring drug efficacy from an attractive model.
+How can a learned weather forecast be evaluated when extreme events are rare?	Inspect hindcast separation, lead times, spatial scales and tail-event metrics in original evaluations; distinguish average skill from reliable local emergency guidance.
+Why can a scientific surrogate model violate a conservation law despite a small average error?	Compare pointwise fit with mass or energy balance in a documented simulation task; test out-of-domain inputs without claiming the surrogate replaces all physical validation.
+What changes when an AI system proposes a molecule rather than demonstrating that it can be made?	Trace generation, synthesis feasibility, actual laboratory validation and selection bias from original reports; exclude chemical synthesis instructions or medical benefit claims.
+# Assistive systems and clinical evaluation boundaries|advanced|health
+How should a screen-description model be evaluated with blind users rather than image-caption scores alone?	Define task completion, navigation, dangerous omissions and consented user feedback; use original assistive-technology studies and avoid treating sighted reviewers as substitutes for intended users.
+Why does retrospective medical-image accuracy not establish improved patient outcomes?	Separate dataset selection, external validation, prospective workflow, clinician behavior and clinical endpoints using original studies; exclude diagnostic advice or a deployment endorsement.
+How can an assistive speech interface accommodate people whose speech differs from its training sample?	Specify speaker-consented evaluation, personalization data, error recovery and task-level success; do not infer a person's competence or medical condition from recognition errors.
+@002
+# Named archaeological identification dossiers|intermediate|history
+How can evidence for Homer's Troy be separated from identification of individual epic events?	Compare Hisarlik excavation phases, dating, place-name arguments and literary chronology; use excavation reports and attributed scholarship without treating a city identification as proof of the entire poem.
+What can excavations at Akrotiri establish about evacuation before the eruption?	Inspect reported finds, missing evidence, stratigraphy and preservation limits; distinguish an absence of recovered victims from proof that every inhabitant escaped.
+How should a film assess different proposed locations for the lost city of Akkad?	Map actual textual references, geographical constraints and excavation evidence in each proposal; retain an unresolved identification rather than choosing by modern visual resemblance.
+What distinguishes evidence for Cahokia's changing population from a sudden-disappearance story?	Compare settlement phases, house counts, environmental data and descendant-community perspectives; avoid replacing one unsupported single-cause collapse narrative with another.
+# Archives reconstructed after destruction|intermediate|history
+How can the pre-destruction contents of the Library of Louvain be reconstructed?	Trace dated catalogs, acquisition records, photographs and surviving volumes through institutional histories; distinguish an item known to have existed from evidence of its exact fate.
+What can surviving finding aids reveal about records lost in Ireland's Public Record Office fire?	Use archival reconstruction projects, pre-fire copies and catalog provenance; mark reconstructed metadata separately from recovered original documents.
+How can displaced Timbuktu manuscript collections be described without revealing sensitive custody details?	Use authorized public collection accounts, catalog records and conservation reports; distinguish digitized access from complete physical survival and omit undisclosed storage locations.
+Why can two catalogs give different identities to the same dispersed manuscript leaf?	Inspect script, dimensions, foliation, text continuity and catalog revision histories for a documented public example; avoid joining fragments on decoration alone.
+# Population and mortality puzzles|advanced|history
+How can underregistration change an apparent historical epidemic mortality rate?	Compare parish registers, burial evidence, population denominators and registration disruptions in one bounded outbreak; use explicit uncertainty rather than extrapolating a precise national total.
+What does the Domesday record omit when used to estimate England's population?	Inspect categories of recorded households, geographic omissions and demographic multipliers; distinguish a fiscal survey's entries from a direct count of all inhabitants.
+How can census boundary changes create an apparent town population collapse?	Reconstruct dated administrative boundaries and enumeration definitions before comparing totals; separate migration, mortality and reclassification rather than choosing one explanation from raw counts.
+How do historians distinguish excess deaths from deaths assigned to a named cause?	Specify a historical baseline, observation window, missing registers and competing classification practices; avoid treating modeled excess mortality as individually documented causes.
+# Revised discoveries and evidence histories|advanced|history
+How did evidence about Sutton Hoo develop beyond the first excavation's public story?	Compare excavation records, later conservation, material analysis and dated reinterpretations; retain uncertainty about the burial's identity rather than presenting a museum label as definitive.
+What changed when later excavations revisited early claims about the site of Knossos?	Separate excavated fabric, reconstruction choices and changing interpretations in traceable archaeological publications; do not substitute a modern reconstruction for a surviving ancient feature.
+How can new dating alter a site narrative without changing the physical finds?	Choose an actual published redating with sample contexts, calibration and alternative chronologies; show which earlier claims depend on the revised date and which remain unaffected.
+@003
+# Regional archaeological sequences and site comparisons|intermediate|history
+How does the sequence at Lahuradewa inform debates about early rice use?	Inspect grain identification, sample context, dates and criteria for cultivation or domestication in excavation and archaeobotanical reports; separate early use from a settled origin claim.
+What can the phases at Chirand reveal about continuity in the middle Ganga region?	Compare published habitation deposits, tools, faunal remains and dating confidence; avoid assigning every phase one unchanging ethnic or linguistic identity.
+How did settlement at Atranjikhera change across its reported ceramic phases?	Follow stratigraphy, iron finds, structures and sample dates in site reports; distinguish ceramic labels from the names of states in later texts.
+What evidence at Hallur links changing crops, animals and metal use?	Compare securely associated finds and dating within the site sequence; do not treat the earliest reported object as a universal date for a technology across India.
+How can Brahmagiri's excavated burials and habitation layers be related cautiously?	Inspect excavation methods, spatial separation, dating and later reassessments; avoid assuming every nearby grave belongs to the same settlement generation.
+What does Sisupalgarh's plan reveal without identifying every building's function?	Use excavation, survey and dated occupation evidence to examine gateways, streets and settlement change; label functional reconstructions and do not infer a complete royal capital from symmetry alone.
+# Inscriptions and coin corpora of specific ruling houses|intermediate|history
+How can the Hathigumpha inscription's damaged passages change a narrative of Kharavela's reign?	Compare published estampages, competing readings, restoration marks and chronological arguments; separate legible statements from reconstructed names or conquests.
+What do the Nasik inscriptions attributed to Gautami Balashri reveal about Satavahana royal memory?	Read the specific inscription with translation, genealogy and rhetorical context; distinguish praise, social claims and independently supported political events.
+How do the Karle donor inscriptions complicate a court-centered history of patronage?	Compile a bounded set of inscriptions with donor names, occupations, places and reading uncertainties; avoid inferring ethnicity or personal belief from a name alone.
+What can the bilingual legends on Indo-Greek coins establish about intended audiences?	Compare named issues, scripts, languages, iconography and secure find information; distinguish communication choices from a census of language speakers.
+How can Kushan coin types be sequenced when find contexts are incomplete?	Inspect die links, overstrikes, legends, hoards and published chronological disagreements; do not equate a deity's appearance with the ruler's exclusive personal faith.
+What does the Eran inscriptional record reveal when read across different monuments?	Keep each inscription's date, patron, physical context and text distinct; avoid fusing several centuries into one event or presenting a disputed reading as universally accepted.
+# Economic and legal vocabulary in context|advanced|history
+How does the meaning of bhaga depend on the text and administrative setting?	Compare bounded passages in a traceable Sanskrit text and inscriptional examples with commentary; do not translate the term as one constant tax rate across all ancient India.
+What can vishti references establish about compulsory labor and its exemptions?	Inspect actual grant clauses, recipients, dates and scholarly interpretations; distinguish the existence of an obligation from evidence of how often it was enforced.
+Why do nivartana and other land measures resist a single modern conversion?	Collect region- and period-specific uses with survey assumptions; present ranges or unknowns rather than a false universal hectare equivalent.
+What rights could an agrahara grant describe without transferring every form of authority?	Read one charter's fiscal, judicial, boundary and exemption clauses in a named edition; distinguish textual grants from evidence of practical control or displacement.
+How do gana and shreni differ across actual inscriptional usages?	Compare explicit contexts, group activities and translations instead of assigning modern corporate or democratic institutions from vocabulary alone.
+# Transmission through named language traditions|advanced|history
+What can disagreements among Arthashastra manuscripts reveal about the history of its text?	Use a critical edition's apparatus, manuscript descriptions and editorial rationale; distinguish textual strata arguments from a proven date for every passage.
+How should the Pali chronicles be compared with inscriptions when reconstructing Ashoka's memory?	Choose specific passages, composition contexts and dated inscriptions; separate later religious historiography from contemporary administrative evidence.
+What can a Prakrit inscription preserve that disappears in a Sanskrit-only historical survey?	Compare one regional corpus's language, formulae, donors and translations; avoid treating language choice as an automatic measure of social rank or literacy.
+How did commentaries change the questions later readers asked of an ancient mathematical text?	Follow one worked problem across the root text and named commentary using traceable editions; distinguish commentator additions from the original author's stated method.
+# Women, work and unequal visibility in source corpora|advanced|history
+How do women donors at Sanchi appear differently from women in normative legal texts?	Compare a defined inscription sample with bounded prescriptive passages; separate recorded donations, legal ideals and unknowable everyday practice.
+What does the Periplus disclose about coastal work while leaving workers unnamed?	Read a specified translation alongside local material evidence on production and exchange; avoid turning an outsider merchant account into the voice of all residents.
+How can spindle whorls inform labor history without assigning every object to women?	Inspect context, use-wear, experimental comparisons and household distribution; distinguish a possible craft activity from the gender or status of its practitioner.
+What can ancient medical case descriptions reveal about social assumptions rather than treatment effectiveness?	Choose public textual passages with edition, translation and historical commentary; examine categories and access while excluding medical recommendations.
+@004
+# Purana-specific dossiers and comparison methods|foundation|tradition
+How should the title Bhagavata be resolved before comparing two sacred narratives?	Identify the exact work, recension, passage, language and translation before discussing the Bhagavata Purana or Devi Bhagavata; do not merge similarly named works into one source.
+How does the Devi Mahatmya organize its three narrative cycles?	Outline the named textual divisions and speakers using a traceable edition; distinguish the narrative's own structure from later performance arrangements or ritual instructions.
+How can a Varaha narrative be compared between two named Puranas without constructing a composite story?	Select exact passages and compare setting, speakers, sequence and attributed theology; label source differences and avoid calling one text a universal final account.
+What does a Purana's frame dialogue contribute beyond introducing its stories?	Track who asks, who answers, where the telling occurs and how authority is established in one specified Purana; do not assume all chapters share one compositional setting.
+# Distinct deity and avatar source files|intermediate|tradition
+How does the Bhagavata Purana's Vamana episode frame Bali's promise and surrender?	Follow the episode in a named edition with passage locators and an attributed commentary; preserve narrative tensions rather than reducing the story to a rule about worldly success.
+How is Narasimha's appearance connected with Prahlada's testimony in a specified source?	Trace the stated boon, confrontation and aftermath in the selected text; check form-specific imagery separately and avoid blending later regional episodes silently.
+What does the Kurma episode contribute to a particular account of the ocean churning?	Compare the avatar's role with the participants, objects and narrative order of one named Purana; distinguish symbolic interpretations from details actually present in the passage.
+How do Savitri's arguments develop during her encounter with Yama in the Mahabharata?	Read the sequence of requests and responses in a specified edition; preserve the character's reasoning and avoid presenting the narrative as a guaranteed longevity practice.
+How is Ganga's descent narrated through the roles of Bhagiratha, Shiva and the river herself?	Use one named Ramayana or Purana passage as the principal account and label variants; distinguish sacred narrative from historical river geology.
+# Ramayana episodes beyond the central battle|intermediate|tradition
+What does Urmila's presence and absence reveal across two named Ramayana retellings?	Verify actual passages and narrative omissions in each text; attribute later elaborations and do not invent a speech to fill a silence in the chosen source.
+How does Guha's encounter with Rama frame friendship and hospitality?	Trace dialogue and actions in a specified Valmiki edition before comparing a regional devotional reading; avoid treating a literary social category as a modern community census.
+What role does Sampati play in turning the search for Sita toward Lanka?	Follow the search party's knowledge before and after his account; distinguish reported information, character inference and later visual additions.
+How does Trijata's dream function inside the narrative rather than as a general dream-prediction manual?	Locate the episode, speaker and audience in the chosen edition; compare the reassurance it offers with later interpretations without endorsing divination claims.
+What does Mandodari's lament ask an audience to reconsider about Ravana?	Use actual speeches and their setting in a named text; preserve grief and moral complexity without rewriting the antagonist's actions or imposing one modern judgment.
+How can an Uttara Kanda retelling disclose edition and reception debates respectfully?	Identify the chosen text's inclusion, scholarly apparatus and distinct devotional reception; separate textual-critical questions from a verdict on a community's faith.
+# Mahabharata dialogues, witnesses and aftermath|intermediate|tradition
+How does the Sulabha-Janaka dialogue examine identity and authority?	Read the complete bounded dialogue in a specified translation and commentary; keep philosophical terms contextual and avoid reducing the exchange to a modern slogan.
+What choices does Kunti describe when Karna learns about his birth?	Follow the encounter's timing, requests and responses in one edition; label later dramatizations and preserve the distinction between narrated knowledge and audience knowledge.
+How does Gandhari's grief shape the Mahabharata's account of victory?	Trace selected postwar passages and their speakers; avoid editing a lament into an uncomplicated endorsement of any side.
+What does the mongoose episode question about the meaning of giving?	Read the episode within its narrative setting and compare one attributed interpretation; distinguish its ethical contrast from a prescription for household donations.
+How do accounts of Abhimanyu's death distribute knowledge and responsibility among characters?	Use a specified edition to track who knows the formation, actions and reported events; exclude unsupported claims about prenatal learning as established science.
+# Regional-language devotional canons|intermediate|tradition
+How does an Andal hymn address the divine differently from a prose biography of Andal?	Identify one hymn, its Tamil text, translation and authorized public commentary; separate the poem's voice from later hagiographic episodes.
+What does a selected Nammalvar verse reveal when read with its traditional commentary?	Bound the episode to one verse and named commentary, explaining key Tamil terms; avoid claiming that one English rendering contains every theological meaning.
+How do Appar and Sambandar describe the same sacred place in selected Tevaram hymns?	Verify hymn attribution, place and translation for both selections; preserve distinct poetic situations rather than presenting all Shaiva hymns as interchangeable.
+How can a Tukaram abhang be interpreted when modern song performances alter its wording?	Compare a traceable Marathi text, attributed translation and the actual performance transcript; verify adaptation rights and do not treat a popular recording as the textual edition.
+What should a Kabir episode disclose about competing collections and attributions?	Identify the exact collection and verse witnesses, compare an attributed translation and preserve uncertainty; avoid assigning every circulating couplet to Kabir.
+# Festivals, narrative variants and iconographic attributes|advanced|community
+How do public accounts of Onam frame Mahabali's return in different Kerala communities?	Use authorized community accounts and source-specific narrative references; distinguish contemporary festival meaning from proof of a single historical origin.
+How do Vishu and a New Year festival elsewhere differ in calendar logic and public symbolism?	Check the particular region, year and official or community calendar before comparison; do not assume every Hindu New Year falls on one date or carries the same narrative.
+What distinguishes an Ashta Lakshmi grouping from one universal eight-form list?	Compare a specified public temple or textual system, names and attributes; label regional variation and do not impose one image's objects on all Lakshmi forms.
+How can a Panchamukhi Hanuman illustration identify its five faces without conflating regional arrangements?	Choose a documented public iconographic reference, record orientation and attributes, and distinguish the selected convention from other depictions; exclude restricted ritual material.
+How do Ardhanarishvara images encode the two sides through clothing, gesture and companions?	Inspect named dated images with museum or temple documentation and compare a public iconographic text; separate observed details from features reconstructed by a modern artist.
+@005
+# Documentary form case studies with accessible evidence|intermediate|media
+How can a one-location documentary build a sequence when movement is limited?	Design an original authorized observation using changing tasks, time, sound and participant choices; assess comprehension in a rough cut without manufacturing conflict.
+What does a desktop documentary need to establish when its action occurs through screens?	Plan provenance for screen recordings, chronology, interface changes and access permissions; distinguish original capture from recreated interfaces and fictional notifications.
+How can a documentary using only still photographs make time understandable?	Storyboard an original rights-cleared sequence with dated images, contextual gaps and narration; disclose camera moves and avoid implying that adjacent photographs show consecutive moments.
+What changes when a radio documentary becomes a captioned video essay?	Compare evidence carried by sound, newly added images and accessibility needs; verify each image's relationship to the claim rather than filling every pause with unrelated stock footage.
+# Archive license contexts and delivery versions|advanced|media
+How should a worldwide online release be checked against an archive license limited to festival screenings?	Read an actual authorized sample license's medium, territory, term and promotional uses; identify questions for the rights holder rather than offering a legal clearance opinion.
+What must be tracked when one archival clip appears in the film, trailer and vertical teaser?	Build a use-level ledger for duration, placement, crop, audio and distribution version; distinguish clearance for the master film from permissions for separate promotional assets.
+How can an archive quotation remain traceable after an image is cropped or colorized?	Retain source asset, modification history, original frame and contextual annotation; label editorial transformations and do not imply colorization recovers exact historical colors.
+What changes when a documentary distributor requests a version without one licensed song?	Trace affected scenes, stems, captions, cue sheets, timing and alternate exports; preserve factual continuity and verify permissions for replacement music separately.
+# Source-language interviews and translation decisions|intermediate|community
+How should a bilingual interview transcript represent code-switching and untranslatable terms?	Retain source-language timecodes, original words, proposed renderings and translator notes; distinguish explanatory glosses from words actually spoken.
+What can back-translation reveal and miss in a sensitive interview passage?	Compare independent translations with a qualified source-language review and surrounding conversation; do not treat agreement between English versions as proof of cultural accuracy.
+How can subtitles preserve a speaker's uncertainty under tight reading-time limits?	Compare source audio, literal transcript and shortened subtitle alternatives; protect hedges, attribution and negation before removing secondary phrasing.
+Who should review a translated interview when the local interpreter is also part of the dispute?	Map disclosed interests, independent language review and participant safety with consent; distinguish translation verification from deciding which account is true.
+# Editing experiments that preserve factual meaning|advanced|media
+How can a documentary test whether a reaction shot falsely implies a response to another event?	Build paired original edits with recorded chronology and ask viewers what caused the reaction; remove an unsupported connection even if it improves dramatic pacing.
+What changes when several pauses are removed from an answer about uncertainty?	Compare the full answer, transcript, edited rhythm and perceived confidence; distinguish ordinary compression from an edit that misrepresents the speaker's degree of knowledge.
+How can a timeline graphic distinguish a confirmed date from a date inferred only within a range?	Assign evidence types, intervals and explicit uncertainty to original timeline elements; avoid animating an estimated moment as if a clock recorded it.
+How can an editor keep a composite scene from being mistaken for one continuous event?	Track recording dates, locations and audio provenance across the sequence; use clear transitions or disclosure rather than relying on a generic end-credit disclaimer.
+# Community distribution and continuing accountability|advanced|community
+What should a community screening agreement cover when participants want discussion in their own language?	Plan accessible subtitles, facilitation, consent for recording and clear limits on reuse; distinguish a local screening from unrestricted distribution rights.
+How can a filmmaker preserve a participant's correction request when a distributor controls the released master?	Trace documented concerns, contractual responsibilities, available updates and communication commitments; avoid promising unilateral removal the producer cannot guarantee.
+How can a film's evidence archive remain usable after grant funding ends?	Plan stewardship, formats, access restrictions, costs and a named responsible custodian; distinguish preserving records from retaining participant data indefinitely without purpose.
+@006
