+# Document and spreadsheet failure test sets|intermediate|technical
+How can an invoice-extraction test distinguish a credit note from a normal invoice?	Author fictional paired documents with signed totals, taxes, currency and explicit document type; score extracted fields and downstream sign handling rather than only readable text.
+What should an AI table-extraction test do with a total split across two scanned pages?	Construct an original multipage fixture with carried subtotals, repeated headers and reading-order traps; compare cell structure and arithmetic against an independent answer key.
+How can a spreadsheet assistant be tested on percentages stored as text?	Use a disposable workbook containing numeric percentages, localized text and blanks; inspect formula results and type conversion against manual calculations without altering real financial records.
+What can a hidden-row test reveal about an AI-generated spreadsheet summary?	Create an original workbook with filters, hidden rows and clearly labeled totals; require the tool to state its inclusion rule and compare results with the intended view.
+How can a document-conversion workflow preserve footnote qualifiers attached to a claim?	Build a short original source with endnotes, tables and a qualified statement; verify rendered pages and claim-footnote links rather than judging only extracted body text.
+# Audio, video and creator export diagnostics|intermediate|media
+How can a subtitle workflow detect timing drift in a long recording?	Use consented or original audio with timed markers near the beginning, middle and end; compare exported cues with the exact media timebase and separate transcription errors from synchronization errors.
+What should an AI video-export test measure when frame rate is variable?	Record source timestamps, output metadata and visible synchronization markers using official tool documentation; avoid assuming a nominal frame-rate label proves uniform timing.
+How can an ambient-loop test distinguish a seamless image transition from an audible seam?	Render an original short loop and inspect the boundary in both waveform and frame sequence; assess repeated listening and viewing without declaring a long export verified from one still image.
+How can a generated Hindi voiceover be checked for devotional names and honorifics?	Use a source-language reviewer, an approved word list and actual audio rather than transcript-only scoring; verify voice-use permission and avoid cloning an identifiable person's voice without consent.
+# Reproducible migrations and changing providers|advanced|technical
+How can an embedding-index migration be tested when the new vectors have a different dimension?	Keep original documents, chunk IDs, retrieval questions and reference passages; build a separate index using versioned official interfaces and compare results without mixing incompatible vector spaces.
+What should a tool-calling migration test verify about optional and missing arguments?	Use a fictional local service with explicit schemas, nulls and omitted fields; check validated calls and returned outcomes rather than assuming matching function names imply equivalent behavior.
+How can a structured-output migration detect silent changes to dates and decimal numbers?	Build an original fixture with ambiguous dates, locale-specific separators and required types; compare parsed values with the answer key under both providers' documented contracts.
+What data must be preserved before retiring a provider-specific conversation store?	Inventory user-owned source messages, attachments, tool results, access restrictions and export capabilities; distinguish available export evidence from a promise of full portability.
+# Accessibility and multilingual end-to-end validation|advanced|community
+How can a keyboard-only user complete an AI image-generation workflow from prompt to saved file?	Plan a consented task test covering focus order, labels, progress, error recovery and download; inspect the actual versioned interface rather than assuming keyboard access from general accessibility claims.
+How can a screen-reader test reveal missing information in an AI tool's image choices?	Compare spoken labels, card selection, generation status and alternative descriptions in a named version; use intended-user feedback and do not infer accessibility from visual layout alone.
+What can a Hindi-English mixed-script test reveal about a search-and-summary workflow?	Create public or original paired documents, preserve transliteration variants and score retrieval and source attribution separately; avoid generalizing from one dialect or script convention.
+How should an AI tutorial distinguish a tested workflow from a planned one?	Publish a version-and-environment ledger with actual commands, observed failures and reproducibility limits after execution; label every unexecuted step and do not fabricate a success screenshot or timing result.
+@008
+# Worked household calculations with explicit assumptions|foundation|finance
+How does daily versus monthly interest calculation change a hypothetical loan balance?	Define an illustrative principal, dates, rate convention, payment timing and rounding; show an independently recalculated ledger and verify product-specific conventions before applying it to any real contract.
+What happens when an emergency expense arrives just before an annual insurance premium?	Build a fictional month-by-month cash calendar separating earmarked funds, liquid balances and due dates; compare scenarios without claiming one reserve amount suits every household.
+How can equal monthly contributions produce different outcomes when returns arrive in a different order?	Use transparent fictional return sequences, contribution dates and fees; distinguish the arithmetic of accumulation from a forecast of market performance.
+What does a tax deduction save when the deduction amount differs from the tax reduction?	Use a labeled hypothetical marginal-rate example and separately verify the chosen jurisdiction's actual rules before scripting; exclude personal eligibility conclusions.
+How can inflation affect a fixed education goal when school costs grow differently from general prices?	Model separate cost growth, saving periods and shortfall sensitivity using hypothetical numbers; do not treat a national price index as a forecast of one institution's fees.
+# India-specific product and disclosure dossiers|intermediate|finance
+What should a bank-deposit protection explainer verify about one depositor holding several accounts?	Read current DICGC official definitions, institution coverage and aggregation examples with an as-of date; distinguish the general framework from a guarantee about a particular failure or payout.
+How can a loan's Key Facts Statement be compared with the repayment schedule?	Use a rights-cleared current sample and official RBI requirements to trace APR, fees, installments and contingent charges; do not infer full compliance from a single matching number.
+What should a mutual-fund Riskometer explanation inspect beyond the color shown in an advertisement?	Check current SEBI requirements, the actual scheme disclosure, date and change history; distinguish a risk classification from a promise about future losses or returns.
+How can a health-insurance co-payment clause change a hypothetical claim payment?	Read the precise policy wording and current IRDAI framework, then calculate one fictional claim with limits and exclusions visible; do not promise approval for an actual medical bill.
+What does a credit-bureau dispute require a consumer explainer to verify?	Use current official bureau and regulator procedures, correction responsibilities and timelines; keep example records fictional and separate a dispute request from guaranteed score improvement.
+# Cross-border household finance|intermediate|finance
+How can a remittance quote hide costs in the exchange rate rather than a stated fee?	Compare simultaneous dated provider disclosures with a declared reference rate and recipient deductions; label the example and avoid presenting an expired quote as available pricing.
+Why can moving abroad change which questions to ask about an Indian bank account?	Use current RBI and bank official materials on residency classification, permitted accounts and documentation; exclude determining any viewer's residency or recommending evasion.
+How can a household compare foreign-currency income with home-currency obligations?	Build explicit exchange-rate scenarios, transfer timing and cash buffers using fictional amounts; distinguish managing a mismatch from speculating on future exchange rates.
+What should be checked when a pension contributor has worked in two countries?	Identify the actual countries, official social-security agreement, covered benefits and qualifying records; do not imply every contribution transfers or that tax treatment follows benefit eligibility.
+How can cross-border inheritance involve separate questions about succession, account access and tax?	Map the relevant jurisdictions and official information sources with a fictional estate; avoid a universal answer or legal instructions for a real family.
+# Consumer disputes and product-document case files|advanced|finance
+How can a household document a disputed card charge without exposing the full card number?	Use current issuer and official dispute instructions, a fictional evidence timeline and redaction checks; distinguish unauthorized use, merchant disputes and refund delays.
+What does an insurance grievance outcome establish about the specific wording of a policy?	Read a public official decision with facts, policy clauses, procedural status and dates; do not treat one decision as a promise for every similar claim.
+How can a mis-selling complaint distinguish an advertisement from the signed product disclosure?	Trace a hypothetical sales timeline with consented or fictional evidence, representations and actual terms; verify the relevant official route without deciding liability.
+What should a failed digital-payment explainer verify before quoting a reversal deadline?	Identify the exact transaction type, failure stage, regulator rule and dated provider procedure; distinguish debited-but-uncredited cases from transfers completed to an unintended recipient.
+# Care, disability and household transitions|advanced|finance
+How can disability-related recurring costs change an otherwise ordinary household budget?	Use consented needs assessment or a fictional case separating access costs, maintenance, support and irregular expenses; avoid assigning one cost profile to everyone with a disability.
+What financial access problems can arise when a sole account holder becomes temporarily unable to act?	Map official bank procedures and legal-authority questions in a hypothetical jurisdiction-specific case; do not recommend password sharing as a substitute for valid authority.
+How can siblings plan shared caregiving costs when their incomes and available time differ?	Compare explicit fictional arrangements for cash, time, transport and recordkeeping; distinguish a negotiated household arrangement from a legal duty or a universally fair formula.
+How can a survivor's short-term cash needs differ from the value of an inherited property?	Build a fictional timeline of bills, access restrictions, estate obligations and illiquid assets; verify legal details before publication and exclude advice to dispose of a specific asset.
+@009
+# Construct dossiers and replication boundaries|foundation|science
+What does the Stroop task measure when reading skill and language differ across participants?	Inspect stimulus design, response time, accuracy and original cross-language studies; distinguish task interference from a general measure of intelligence or willpower.
+How can a stop-signal task estimate response inhibition without observing an internal stop process directly?	Trace the task model, assumptions, failed stopping and estimation method in primary research; avoid turning a task estimate into a diagnosis or global self-control score.
+What do the original marshmallow-delay studies establish separately from later follow-up associations?	Compare samples, procedures, predictive models and later contextual analyses; distinguish a childhood task from a deterministic forecast of adult success.
+How can an ego-depletion claim be examined across different tasks and replication designs?	Use original protocols, preregistered replications and effect estimates; separate a disputed mechanism from the ordinary experience of fatigue.
+What does growth-mindset research require beyond comparing favorable beliefs with grades?	Inspect intervention content, randomization, subgroup specification and educational context in original trials; avoid a universal promise that changing beliefs removes structural barriers.
+# Specific perception and cognition experiments|intermediate|science
+How does the McGurk effect depend on the particular sound and visual stimulus?	Use licensed or original demonstrations with appropriate consent and primary studies of variation; distinguish a striking audiovisual illusion from failure of hearing generally.
+What can change-blindness experiments reveal when attention and memory demands are separated?	Compare interruption, scene complexity and detection measures with an original protocol; exclude identifying one individual's attentional capacity from an online demonstration.
+How does signal-detection theory separate sensitivity from willingness to say yes?	Work through explicit hypothetical hit and false-alarm rates with an adjustable criterion; distinguish the model from a diagnosis of honesty or confidence.
+What do serial-position experiments reveal when rehearsal and delay change?	Compare immediate and delayed list recall with controlled word familiarity; distinguish descriptive primacy and recency patterns from proof of one unique memory architecture.
+How can mental-rotation experiments distinguish task strategy from a fixed spatial ability?	Inspect stimulus type, practice, accuracy and response-time patterns in primary reports; avoid ranking genders or cultures from one task sample.
+# Lifespan and cross-cultural comparison designs|advanced|science
+How can a cohort-sequential study separate aging from generational experience better than one age-group comparison?	Map repeated cohorts, time points, attrition and remaining identification limits; use published design examples rather than interpreting every age difference as decline.
+What must be tested before comparing the same wellbeing scale across languages?	Inspect translation work, item functioning and measurement invariance in original validation studies; distinguish score comparability from a ranking of national happiness.
+How can a developmental task mistake unfamiliar instructions for lack of an underlying ability?	Compare comprehension checks, culturally familiar materials and alternative responses; avoid declaring that a community lacks a cognitive capacity from one failed task.
+Why can parent reports and teacher reports disagree about a child's behavior?	Examine settings, observation opportunities, scale definitions and actual multi-informant studies; do not diagnose a child or assume one reporter is dishonest.
+# Applied domains with defined evidence limits|intermediate|science
+What can retrieval-practice experiments tell a student about studying beyond repeated rereading?	Compare delayed retention, question format, feedback and subject matter in original learning studies; avoid promising identical benefits for every learner or exam.
+How should research on notification interruptions distinguish task delay from lasting attention change?	Use study designs with specified devices, interruption schedules and outcome windows; separate short-term performance from unsupported claims of permanent brain damage.
+What does a choice-architecture experiment need to establish before calling a default beneficial?	Inspect uptake, informed preferences, opt-out burden and measured welfare in a named study; distinguish changed behavior from improved outcomes or consent.
+How can psychological safety in teams be studied without equating it with comfort or agreement?	Compare construct definitions, surveys, observed speaking behavior and organizational context; avoid labeling a real workplace from one anecdote or rating.
+How can a courtroom memory study inform policy without deciding whether one witness is accurate?	Review the exact encoding, delay, identification and confidence conditions in original studies; preserve the gap between population evidence and an individual legal conclusion.
+# Competing theories in their historical experiments|advanced|history
+What did behaviorist and cognitive accounts predict differently about latent learning?	Compare the actual maze designs, reward timing and historical interpretations with original research; avoid portraying either tradition as one unchanging position.
+How did signal-detection approaches change interpretations of an absolute sensory threshold?	Trace the historical measurement problem, decision criterion and experimental evidence; distinguish a theoretical advance from proof that every perception follows the same model.
+What does the James-Lange debate reveal when physiological arousal and reported emotion are measured separately?	Use original formulations and later testable variants; avoid a simplistic account in which one experiment conclusively settled all theories of emotion.
+How can connectionist and symbolic models be compared on the same learning phenomenon?	Define the actual task, representational assumptions, fitting data and held-out predictions using original model papers; separate explanatory comparison from claims about a complete human mind.
+@010
+# Named case dossiers grounded in public findings|intermediate|history
+How can the Guildford Four case be reconstructed through convictions, inquiry findings and later legal outcomes?	Build a dated record from official judgments and public inquiry material, verifying each person's status; attribute allegations and avoid treating a later summary as the original evidentiary record.
+What does the official record of the Post Office Horizon scandal distinguish between software problems and particular convictions?	Use current judgments, inquiry documents and official redress records with dates; retain separate case outcomes and do not imply every affected person followed the same legal route.
+How can the Madoff case distinguish the criminal judgment from recovery of investors' funds?	Read official court and trustee records, separate proven conduct from recovery accounting and date all totals; exclude a promise about any individual's compensation.
+What changed between the original prosecution and later court review in the Sally Clark case?	Compare the actual appellate judgments, statistical reasoning and evidentiary issues; avoid presenting one statistical error as the sole documented reason for every legal outcome.
+# Method-specific forensic controversies|advanced|science
+What does a microscopic hair-comparison opinion establish without DNA confirmation?	Use official method reviews, original validation research and the exact language of a public case opinion; distinguish claimed similarity from individual identification.
+How can a bite-mark evidence episode separate historical testimony from current validation findings?	Trace official reviews, study designs and a dated public case record; avoid reproducing unsupported certainty or diagnosing a mark from an image.
+Why do probabilistic DNA-mixture results depend on competing propositions and modeling choices?	Inspect published validation, stated contributors, assumptions and likelihood-ratio wording; exclude calculating guilt probabilities or analyzing an actual private person's DNA.
+What limits apply when estimating the timing of death from environmental and biological observations?	Compare the documented method, observation window, conditions and uncertainty in primary research or official reports; avoid a precise reenactment clock unsupported by evidence.
+How should a firearm-comparison documentary distinguish examiner conclusions from measured error rates?	Read the exact comparison task, validation design and official terminology; do not extrapolate laboratory results to all weapons, conditions or examiners.
+# Jurisdiction-specific reporting and procedure|advanced|civic
+How does reporting a coroner's inquest differ from reporting a criminal trial?	Choose one jurisdiction and read its official mandate, evidentiary rules, permitted findings and reporting restrictions; do not treat an inquest conclusion as a criminal conviction.
+What should be checked before naming a juvenile involved in a publicized case?	Verify current jurisdiction-specific anonymity rules, court orders and procedural status through official sources; avoid assuming social-media circulation removes legal or ethical protections.
+How can an extradition judgment be explained without implying it decides guilt on the underlying charge?	Read the precise court's powers, issues, order and appeal status; distinguish surrender conditions from adjudication of the alleged conduct.
+What can a civil damages judgment establish separately from a criminal verdict about related events?	Compare parties, causes of action, proof standards and actual findings in one named jurisdiction; avoid importing language from one proceeding into the other.
+# Institutional response and affected-community evidence|advanced|community
+How can a documentary assess repeated investigative failures identified by an official inquiry?	Trace each documented failure, organizational response, recommendation and follow-up evidence; distinguish inquiry findings from unsupported blame against individual workers.
+What does a victim-notification policy reveal when compared with documented implementation?	Use current official procedures and consented participant accounts with dates and redaction; do not infer every family's experience from one public complaint.
+How can a documentary include defense investigators' work without endorsing every proposed alternative theory?	Check each claim against the public record, case status and independent evidence; distinguish a reasonable question from an established account of what happened.
+How can a prison-death documentary center an official investigation without erasing the person's life?	Compare public findings, family-consented biography and documented custody responsibilities; omit graphic detail without explanatory value and avoid diagnosing intent from incomplete records.
+# Corrections across reused evidence and released versions|advanced|media
+What should happen when a forensic method featured in an older episode receives a major official reassessment?	Trace the exact original claim, new review, affected case status and all reused clips; correct implications proportionately without asserting that every conviction using the method is invalid.
+How can a true-crime channel distinguish a family's request to remove imagery from a factual correction?	Record the concern, existing permissions, editorial purpose and available remedies; preserve respectful communication without promising that consent alone resolves every publication issue.
+How can a case-status update avoid redistributing a defamatory older title through its own correction?	Review the revised wording, thumbnails, excerpts and search descriptions with current legal findings; explain the corrected status without reusing an unsupported allegation as promotion.
+What should a source appendix do when a public court document is later sealed or redacted?	Verify current access restrictions and applicable official rules, preserve an internal audit trail where lawful, and remove restricted identifying details; do not mirror inaccessible sensitive records merely because they were once public.
