+**21 categories · 104 individually authored episode proposals.**
 
 Individually authored episode questions and coverage boundaries for AI Tools / AI Tutorials. The subject progression is organized by concrete content rather than a topic-by-angle multiplication.
 
@@ -235,6 +235,72 @@ Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources
 | BANK-007-094 | What should a creator test before moving a content pipeline to a new provider? | Compare required features, output compatibility, rights and complete representative runs. |
 | BANK-007-095 | How can an AI tutorial be corrected when a previously free capability becomes paid? | Date the change, update the workflow and distinguish historical instructions from current availability. |
 
+## 17. Named local-runtime tutorial plans
+
+**Level:** foundation. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-007-096 | How can an Ollama tutorial test model availability separately from chat-template behavior? | At production, record the actual Ollama version, official model documentation, local list and a minimal request using harmless text; plan separate checks for model loading and role formatting rather than assuming every model supports identical options. |
+| BANK-007-097 | How can a llama.cpp tutorial verify that its selected backend is actually doing the computation? | Pin the tested release, build options, hardware and official logs; compare a small controlled run and resource evidence without using a GPU usage screenshot alone as proof of complete offload. |
+| BANK-007-098 | What should an LM Studio model-import lesson verify before declaring a downloaded file compatible? | Record application version, model architecture, file provenance and official supported-runtime guidance; keep the proposed steps provisional until executed on the specified system. |
+| BANK-007-099 | How can a Whisper transcription lesson expose errors that a fluent paragraph conceals? | Use licensed or consented audio with an aligned reference including names, numbers and overlapping speech; record the exact implementation, model and language settings without claiming a successful test before running it. |
+
+## 18. Document and spreadsheet failure test sets
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-007-100 | How can an invoice-extraction test distinguish a credit note from a normal invoice? | Author fictional paired documents with signed totals, taxes, currency and explicit document type; score extracted fields and downstream sign handling rather than only readable text. |
+| BANK-007-101 | What should an AI table-extraction test do with a total split across two scanned pages? | Construct an original multipage fixture with carried subtotals, repeated headers and reading-order traps; compare cell structure and arithmetic against an independent answer key. |
+| BANK-007-102 | How can a spreadsheet assistant be tested on percentages stored as text? | Use a disposable workbook containing numeric percentages, localized text and blanks; inspect formula results and type conversion against manual calculations without altering real financial records. |
+| BANK-007-103 | What can a hidden-row test reveal about an AI-generated spreadsheet summary? | Create an original workbook with filters, hidden rows and clearly labeled totals; require the tool to state its inclusion rule and compare results with the intended view. |
+| BANK-007-104 | How can a document-conversion workflow preserve footnote qualifiers attached to a claim? | Build a short original source with endnotes, tables and a qualified statement; verify rendered pages and claim-footnote links rather than judging only extracted body text. |
+
+## 19. Audio, video and creator export diagnostics
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-007-105 | How can a subtitle workflow detect timing drift in a long recording? | Use consented or original audio with timed markers near the beginning, middle and end; compare exported cues with the exact media timebase and separate transcription errors from synchronization errors. |
+| BANK-007-106 | What should an AI video-export test measure when frame rate is variable? | Record source timestamps, output metadata and visible synchronization markers using official tool documentation; avoid assuming a nominal frame-rate label proves uniform timing. |
+| BANK-007-107 | How can an ambient-loop test distinguish a seamless image transition from an audible seam? | Render an original short loop and inspect the boundary in both waveform and frame sequence; assess repeated listening and viewing without declaring a long export verified from one still image. |
+| BANK-007-108 | How can a generated Hindi voiceover be checked for devotional names and honorifics? | Use a source-language reviewer, an approved word list and actual audio rather than transcript-only scoring; verify voice-use permission and avoid cloning an identifiable person's voice without consent. |
+
+## 20. Reproducible migrations and changing providers
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the actual system documentation, a worked implementation and measurements. Identify inputs, outputs, constraints, tolerances, failure conditions and the limits of the example. Do not provide hazardous construction or unauthorized access procedures.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original engineering papers; official versioned product or standards documentation; test reports and drawings with clear provenance. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-007-109 | How can an embedding-index migration be tested when the new vectors have a different dimension? | Keep original documents, chunk IDs, retrieval questions and reference passages; build a separate index using versioned official interfaces and compare results without mixing incompatible vector spaces. |
+| BANK-007-110 | What should a tool-calling migration test verify about optional and missing arguments? | Use a fictional local service with explicit schemas, nulls and omitted fields; check validated calls and returned outcomes rather than assuming matching function names imply equivalent behavior. |
+| BANK-007-111 | How can a structured-output migration detect silent changes to dates and decimal numbers? | Build an original fixture with ambiguous dates, locale-specific separators and required types; compare parsed values with the answer key under both providers' documented contracts. |
+| BANK-007-112 | What data must be preserved before retiring a provider-specific conversation store? | Inventory user-owned source messages, attachments, tool results, access restrictions and export capabilities; distinguish available export evidence from a promise of full portability. |
