+| BANK-007-114 | How can a screen-reader test reveal missing information in an AI tool's image choices? | Compare spoken labels, card selection, generation status and alternative descriptions in a named version; use intended-user feedback and do not infer accessibility from visual layout alone. |
+| BANK-007-115 | What can a Hindi-English mixed-script test reveal about a search-and-summary workflow? | Create public or original paired documents, preserve transliteration variants and score retrieval and source attribution separately; avoid generalizing from one dialect or script convention. |
+| BANK-007-116 | How should an AI tutorial distinguish a tested workflow from a planned one? | Publish a version-and-environment ledger with actual commands, observed failures and reproducibility limits after execution; label every unexecuted step and do not fabricate a success screenshot or timing result. |
