@@ -262,6 +262,72 @@ Every question below has its own coverage boundary. All remain proposed; sources
 | BANK-010-103 | What should a creator measure before claiming a series improved public understanding? | Use ethical audience research and concrete knowledge outcomes rather than views alone. |
 | BANK-010-104 | How can a final episode distinguish narrative closure from legal or historical resolution? | State the actual outcome, remaining uncertainties and whose experience continues beyond the film. |
 
+## 19. Named case dossiers grounded in public findings
+
+**Level:** intermediate. **Evidence direction:** Compare dated primary records, material evidence and historical scholarship. Distinguish event dates, the dates of surviving witnesses, later retellings and disagreement. Do not invent quotations, intentions or an unbroken lineage.
+
+**Source types to locate:** dated archival records and original publications; inscriptions, artifacts or photographs with provenance; critical editions and historical scholarship. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-010-105 | How can the Guildford Four case be reconstructed through convictions, inquiry findings and later legal outcomes? | Build a dated record from official judgments and public inquiry material, verifying each person's status; attribute allegations and avoid treating a later summary as the original evidentiary record. |
+| BANK-010-106 | What does the official record of the Post Office Horizon scandal distinguish between software problems and particular convictions? | Use current judgments, inquiry documents and official redress records with dates; retain separate case outcomes and do not imply every affected person followed the same legal route. |
+| BANK-010-107 | How can the Madoff case distinguish the criminal judgment from recovery of investors' funds? | Read official court and trustee records, separate proven conduct from recovery accounting and date all totals; exclude a promise about any individual's compensation. |
+| BANK-010-108 | What changed between the original prosecution and later court review in the Sally Clark case? | Compare the actual appellate judgments, statistical reasoning and evidentiary issues; avoid presenting one statistical error as the sole documented reason for every legal outcome. |
+
+## 20. Method-specific forensic controversies
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use original observations or experiments, an appropriate scientific reference and the actual measurement method. Distinguish mechanisms, correlations, model assumptions, uncertainty and limits of generalization.
+
+**Source types to locate:** original research reports and data; research-institution observation records; methods papers and current scientific reference works. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-010-109 | What does a microscopic hair-comparison opinion establish without DNA confirmation? | Use official method reviews, original validation research and the exact language of a public case opinion; distinguish claimed similarity from individual identification. |
+| BANK-010-110 | How can a bite-mark evidence episode separate historical testimony from current validation findings? | Trace official reviews, study designs and a dated public case record; avoid reproducing unsupported certainty or diagnosing a mark from an image. |
+| BANK-010-111 | Why do probabilistic DNA-mixture results depend on competing propositions and modeling choices? | Inspect published validation, stated contributors, assumptions and likelihood-ratio wording; exclude calculating guilt probabilities or analyzing an actual private person's DNA. |
+| BANK-010-112 | What limits apply when estimating the timing of death from environmental and biological observations? | Compare the documented method, observation window, conditions and uncertainty in primary research or official reports; avoid a precise reenactment clock unsupported by evidence. |
+| BANK-010-113 | How should a firearm-comparison documentary distinguish examiner conclusions from measured error rates? | Read the exact comparison task, validation design and official terminology; do not extrapolate laboratory results to all weapons, conditions or examiners. |
+
+## 21. Jurisdiction-specific reporting and procedure
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use the current official legal text, policy, procedure or public dataset for a specific jurisdiction and date. Distinguish written rules, implementation and lived access; give no personal legal or financial conclusion.
+
+**Source types to locate:** official laws, rules and administrative guidance; audits, judgments and public service records; consented accounts from affected people and qualified specialists. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-010-114 | How does reporting a coroner's inquest differ from reporting a criminal trial? | Choose one jurisdiction and read its official mandate, evidentiary rules, permitted findings and reporting restrictions; do not treat an inquest conclusion as a criminal conviction. |
+| BANK-010-115 | What should be checked before naming a juvenile involved in a publicized case? | Verify current jurisdiction-specific anonymity rules, court orders and procedural status through official sources; avoid assuming social-media circulation removes legal or ethical protections. |
+| BANK-010-116 | How can an extradition judgment be explained without implying it decides guilt on the underlying charge? | Read the precise court's powers, issues, order and appeal status; distinguish surrender conditions from adjudication of the alleged conduct. |
+| BANK-010-117 | What can a civil damages judgment establish separately from a criminal verdict about related events? | Compare parties, causes of action, proof standards and actual findings in one named jurisdiction; avoid importing language from one proceeding into the other. |
+
+## 22. Institutional response and affected-community evidence
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Use consented participant accounts, local records and the community's own descriptions. Include differences of position, access and power; testimony is not a representative survey or clinical proof.
+
+**Source types to locate:** consented interviews and oral histories; community publications and local records; field notes with method and consent documented. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-010-118 | How can a documentary assess repeated investigative failures identified by an official inquiry? | Trace each documented failure, organizational response, recommendation and follow-up evidence; distinguish inquiry findings from unsupported blame against individual workers. |
+| BANK-010-119 | What does a victim-notification policy reveal when compared with documented implementation? | Use current official procedures and consented participant accounts with dates and redaction; do not infer every family's experience from one public complaint. |
+| BANK-010-120 | How can a documentary include defense investigators' work without endorsing every proposed alternative theory? | Check each claim against the public record, case status and independent evidence; distinguish a reasonable question from an established account of what happened. |
+| BANK-010-121 | How can a prison-death documentary center an official investigation without erasing the person's life? | Compare public findings, family-consented biography and documented custody responsibilities; omit graphic detail without explanatory value and avoid diagnosing intent from incomplete records. |
+
+## 23. Corrections across reused evidence and released versions
+
+**Level:** advanced. **Evidence direction:** Analyze an identifiable work or create a clearly labeled original example. Connect creative decisions to observable audience information; respect rights, attribution, consent and the difference between intent and reception.
+
+**Source types to locate:** the actual work and authorized production materials; creator interviews or published craft explanations; permission-cleared examples and audience feedback. These are requirements, not sources already inspected.
+
+| ID | Specific episode question | Individually written scope and exclusions |
+|---|---|---|
+| BANK-010-122 | What should happen when a forensic method featured in an older episode receives a major official reassessment? | Trace the exact original claim, new review, affected case status and all reused clips; correct implications proportionately without asserting that every conviction using the method is invalid. |
+| BANK-010-123 | How can a true-crime channel distinguish a family's request to remove imagery from a factual correction? | Record the concern, existing permissions, editorial purpose and available remedies; preserve respectful communication without promising that consent alone resolves every publication issue. |
+| BANK-010-124 | How can a case-status update avoid redistributing a defamatory older title through its own correction? | Review the revised wording, thumbnails, excerpts and search descriptions with current legal findings; explain the corrected status without reusing an unsupported allegation as promotion. |
+| BANK-010-125 | What should a source appendix do when a public court document is later sealed or redacted? | Verify current access restrictions and applicable official rules, preserve an internal audit trail where lawful, and remove restricted identifying details; do not mirror inaccessible sensitive records merely because they were once public. |
+
 ## Coverage limits and next step
 
 This is an expanded topic-bank draft, not exhaustive scholarship or a researched episode package. Each question has an individually written boundary. Source access, claim verification, current angle-scope review and publication approval remain pending. Add new branches and cases when they fill a real gap; no numeric topic cap applies.
